<%#
  Entry-confirmed celebration — now a THIN ADAPTER over the ENGINE's card
  (studio/modals/blocks/_entry_confirmed, studio-engine >= 0.62.2).

  This file was a 219-line FORK. The divergence was always smaller than that
  number suggested: turf hand-rolled the spine (card_header + solana_tx_link +
  cta_redirect directly) where the engine composes _success_card, and its
  animated seeds block was a fork of the engine's blocks/_seeds_bar. The engine
  now carries every seam this app needed, so what is left here is the mapping.

  WHY EACH LOCAL IS PASSED — none of these is a default:

    props_expr        $store.solanaModal is a DIRECT-FIELD store with no
                      .current(). The engine's default reads
                      $store.<modal_store>.current().props, which on this app
                      resolves to {} and would render the card complete with
                      none of its numbers.

    title_key         PINNED to the literal 'Good Luck'. The engine default is
                      "props.title || 'Good Luck'", and this store DOES carry a
                      .title — it holds the PROCESSING headline ("Confirming…").
                      Letting the default run would put that on the success card.

    cluster_param     The engine defaults to "" which is MAINNET. Omitting it on
                      a devnet deploy points the explorer link at a chain that
                      has never seen the transaction.

    cta_label         The literal emoji, not the HTML entities the fork used.
                      _success_card prints the label through a normal escaping
                      output tag, so entities would appear on the button as
                      visible text rather than as a glyph.
                      (Describing that tag in words on purpose: quoting it here
                      would end this comment at its close sequence and leak the
                      rest of the prose into the page — the very defect
                      test/lib/erb_comment_percent_test.rb guards, which is how
                      this paragraph got rewritten.)

    secondary_*       Keeps this card's "Dismiss" affordance, which the engine
                      card would otherwise not have. The event is caught on
                      _onchain_tx's root; see the listener there.

    above_seeds       The kickoff countdown, which has no engine equivalent and
                      must render ABOVE the seeds bar. wrapper_class carries the
                      centring that the fork's surrounding <div> used to provide.

  slot_position is NOT passed: the engine already defaults it to :above_cta for
  this card, which is the layout Mr. McRitchie confirmed on 2026-08-26 — kickoff
  and seeds above the button, not below it.
%>
<%
  tx_signature_key = local_assigns.fetch(:tx_signature_key)
  lobby_url_key    = local_assigns.fetch(:lobby_url_key)
  seeds_earned_key = local_assigns.fetch(:seeds_earned_key)
  seeds_total_key  = local_assigns.fetch(:seeds_total_key)
  kickoff_at       = local_assigns[:kickoff_at]

  engine_locals = {
    props_expr:       "$store.solanaModal",
    title_key:        "'Good Luck'",
    subtitle:         "Entry Confirmed",
    tx_signature_key: tx_signature_key,
    lobby_url_key:    lobby_url_key,
    cta_label:        "Contest Lobby ⚔️",
    seeds_earned_key: seeds_earned_key,
    seeds_total_key:  seeds_total_key,
    secondary_label:  "Dismiss",
    secondary_event:  "tm-entry-dismiss"
  }

  # Only when a contest is in scope — a real entry on a contest page. The
  # gallery preview passes no kickoff_at and simply renders without it.
  if kickoff_at.present?
    engine_locals[:above_seeds] = "contests/timestamp_countdown"
    engine_locals[:above_seeds_locals] = {
      target:        kickoff_at,
      label:         "Kicks off in",
      done_label:    "🟢 Contest underway",
      tone:          "yellow",
      wrapper_class: "flex justify-center mb-4"
    }
  end
%>
<%# cluster_param is passed INLINE, not folded into engine_locals above, and that
    is deliberate. test/integration/engine_modal_defork_test.rb scans every
    callsite of an engine Solana block and requires cluster_param to be visible
    in the render call — because the engine defaults it to "" (MAINNET), so a
    callsite that omits it renders an explorer link that resolves, looks
    correct, and finds nothing. Hidden inside a locals hash it is unreadable to
    that guard, and to the next person reading this file. %>
<%= render "studio/modals/blocks/entry_confirmed",
      **engine_locals,
      cluster_param: solana_explorer_cluster_param %>
